            {
                "node": {
                    "created_at": "1775146564",
                    "text": "A data career isn’t a single role anymore.\n\nIt’s an ecosystem.\n\nDifferent layers, different skills, all working together.\n\nHere’s how the modern data world is structured 👇\n\n- Core roles\nTurning data into value through roles like analysts, engineers, and AI builders who handle everything from insights to production systems.\n\n- Data engineering\nMoving, transforming, and preparing data so it’s clean, reliable, and always available for downstream use.\n\n- Data science & ML\nBuilding models that learn patterns, make predictions, and solve complex problems using data.\n\n- Analytics & BI\nPresenting data in a way that drives decisions through dashboards, reports, and business-friendly insights.\n\n- AI & LLM engineering\nCreating intelligent applications using LLMs, agents, embeddings, and modern AI architectures.\n\n- Cloud & infrastructure\nProviding scalable systems and platforms where data storage, processing, and AI workloads run efficiently.\n\n- DataOps & governance\nEnsuring data is accurate, secure, traceable, and compliant across the entire lifecycle.\n\n- Foundation skills\nCore technical skills like SQL, Python, Git, and Linux that support every layer in the data stack.\n\nWhat this means:\nYour role is just one layer.\nYour growth depends on understanding the stack around it.\n\nGo deep in one area.\nStay aware of the entire system.\n\nWhich layer are you building depth in right now?",
                    "id": "18003872213908542"
                }
            }
        ]
    },
